---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="A pool of 4,000 labelled prompts stands for real traffic. Both models are graded pass or fail on the same items. Pick how many items you evaluate and how much better or worse the new model really is, then see how often a release gate gets it wrong.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Defaults (100 items, new model <b>3 points worse</b>, gate <b>ship if new &ge; old</b>): the true gap is <b>&minus;2.5</b> points, yet the gate ships the regression in <b>84 of 300</b> repeated evals (<b>28%</b>), and each 95% interval is about <b>12 points</b> wide. The 20 interval bars below show the same eval set drawn again and again.</li>
    <li>Raise the eval set to <b>1000</b> items: the same regression ships only <b>3 of 300</b> times (<b>1%</b>) and the interval narrows to about <b>4 points</b>. Four times the data does not give four times the sharpness: width shrinks with the square root of the set size.</li>
    <li>Go back to <b>100</b> items, choose the gate <b>Block if lower bound is under -2 pts</b>, and set the change to <b>+3 points</b> (a real win): the regression case is now safe (it ships in about <b>6 of 300</b>), but the true <b>+3.6</b> point win is wrongly blocked in <b>170 of 300</b> evals (<b>56%</b>). A small set cannot prove safety. At <b>1000</b> items it ships <b>300 of 300</b>.</li>
    <li>Set the change to <b>0</b>, the gate to <b>ship only if the lower bound is above 0</b> and the set to <b>2000</b>: a model that is no better still gets through in about <b>16 of 300</b> evals (<b>5%</b>). Run enough evals against one set and some will pass by luck, so re-use of the same set needs a stricter bar.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg mev" data-mev>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Eval set size (items) <select class="pg-in" data-n><option value="25">25</option><option value="50">50</option><option value="100" selected>100</option><option value="200">200</option><option value="500">500</option><option value="1000">1,000</option><option value="2000">2,000</option></select></label>
      <label>Real change in pass rate (points) <input type="range" min="-6" max="6" step="1" value="-3" data-delta /> <b data-deltaval>-3</b></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Release gate <select class="pg-in" data-gate><option value="point" selected>Ship if new &ge; old</option><option value="noninf">Block if lower bound is under -2 pts</option><option value="prove">Ship only if lower bound is above 0</option></select></label>
      <button class="btn" type="button" data-again>Draw another eval set</button>
      <button class="btn" type="button" data-reset>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" role="status" data-verdict></p>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-1)"><h3>This eval set</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-one></span><span class="pg-note" data-onenote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-gatebox style="--c: var(--role-3)"><h3>Wrong calls over 300 evals</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-wrong></span><span class="pg-note" data-wrongnote></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--role-4)"><h3>Interval width</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-width></span><span class="pg-note">average 95% interval over 300 evals</span></div>
    </div>
    <h3>Repeated evals of the same two models</h3>
    <p class="pg-note">Each row is a fresh eval set. The bar is the 95% interval for the pass-rate difference, the dot is the measured difference, the vertical line is zero, the scale runs from -20 to +20 points. Filled bars mean the gate would ship.</p>
    <div class="mev-rows" data-rows role="img" aria-label="Twenty repeated paired evaluations, each drawn as a confidence interval on a scale from minus 20 to plus 20 points"></div>
    <p class="pg-note">Model assumptions: each item has a hidden difficulty; each model passes it when difficulty plus its own run-to-run noise is under a threshold, so the models are strongly correlated and the pairing matters. The old model passes about 68% of the pool. The pool has 4,000 items and every eval draws items from it with replacement, which stands in for sampling real traffic. The interval is the normal approximation on the per-item paired difference, 1.96 standard errors either side. The true gap is measured on all 4,000 items. A change of 1 point or more counts as real, anything smaller counts as noise either way. Seeded, so every number here repeats.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  const POOL = 4000, TRIALS = 300, T_OLD = 700, ROWS = 20, SCALE = 20;
  const POOL_SEED = 20240601;
  const SCORE_RANGE = 1000; const NOISE_SPAN = 301; const NOISE_HALF = 150; // item difficulty 0..999, model noise -150..150
  const SCORE_PER_PT = 10; // one accuracy point moves the threshold by 10 score units
  const Z95 = 1.96; // normal quantile for a 95% interval
  const NONINF_MARGIN = 0.02; // non-inferiority gate tolerates a 2 point drop
  const TRIAL_SEED = { base: 1000, step: 7919 }; const RUN_SEED = { base: 500000, step: 104729 };
  const NOISE_BAND = 0.01; // true gaps inside +-1 point count as no real difference
  const WRONG_DIV = 10; // more than one wrong call in 10 evals marks the gate as bad
  // Park-Miller minimal-standard LCG
  function makePool() {
    let x = POOL_SEED; const r = () => (x = (x * 48271) % 2147483647);
    const z = [], no = [], nn = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < POOL; i++) { z.push(r() % SCORE_RANGE); no.push((r() % NOISE_SPAN) - NOISE_HALF); nn.push((r() % NOISE_SPAN) - NOISE_HALF); }
    return { z, no, nn };
  }
  const P = makePool();
  const cache = new Map();
  function outcomes(deltaPts) {
    if (cache.has(deltaPts)) return cache.get(deltaPts);
    const old = [], nw = []; let so = 0, sn = 0; const shift = deltaPts * SCORE_PER_PT;
    for (let i = 0; i < POOL; i++) {
      const o = P.z[i] + P.no[i] < T_OLD ? 1 : 0; const n = P.z[i] + P.nn[i] < T_OLD + shift ? 1 : 0;
      old.push(o); nw.push(n); so += o; sn += n;
    }
    const res = { old, nw, trueDiff: (sn - so) / POOL, oldRate: so / POOL };
    cache.set(deltaPts, res); return res;
  }
  function evalSet(O, n, seed) {
    let x = seed; const r = () => (x = (x * 48271) % 2147483647);
    let b = 0, c = 0, po = 0, pn = 0;
    for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) {
      const i = r() % POOL; po += O.old[i]; pn += O.nw[i];
      const d = O.nw[i] - O.old[i]; if (d > 0) b++; else if (d < 0) c++;
    }
    const mean = (b - c) / n; const s2 = n > 1 ? (b + c - n * mean * mean) / (n - 1) : 0; const se = Math.sqrt(Math.max(0, s2) / n);
    return { n, b, c, po: po / n, pn: pn / n, mean, lo: mean - Z95 * se, hi: mean + Z95 * se };
  }
  const GATES = { point: (r) => r.mean >= 0, noninf: (r) => r.lo > -NONINF_MARGIN, prove: (r) => r.lo > 0 };
  function study(O, n, gate) {
    let ship = 0, wid = 0;
    for (let t = 0; t < TRIALS; t++) { const r = evalSet(O, n, TRIAL_SEED.base + t * TRIAL_SEED.step); if (GATES[gate](r)) ship++; wid += r.hi - r.lo; }
    return { ship, width: wid / TRIALS };
  }
  const runSeed = (run) => RUN_SEED.base + run * RUN_SEED.step;
  const pts = (v, d = 1) => (v * 100).toFixed(d);
  const signed = (v, d = 1) => (v > 0 ? '+' : '') + (v * 100).toFixed(d);

  document.querySelectorAll('[data-mev]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = (s) => root.querySelector(s);
    const val = (s) => Number(q(s).value);
    let run = 0; let scheduled = false;
    const rowsEl = q('[data-rows]'); const rows = [];
    const pos = (v) => Math.max(0, Math.min(100, 50 + (v * 100 * 50) / SCALE));
    for (let i = 0; i < ROWS; i++) {
      const row = document.createElement('div'); row.className = 'mev-row';
      const lab = document.createElement('span'); lab.className = 'pg-mono mev-lab';
      const track = document.createElement('span'); track.className = 'mev-track';
      const zero = document.createElement('span'); zero.className = 'mev-zero';
      const bar = document.createElement('span'); bar.className = 'mev-bar';
      const dot = document.createElement('span'); dot.className = 'mev-dot';
      track.append(zero, bar, dot); row.append(lab, track); rowsEl.appendChild(row);
      rows.push({ lab, bar, dot });
    }
    function draw() {
      scheduled = false;
      const n = val('[data-n]'); const delta = val('[data-delta]'); const gate = q('[data-gate]').value;
      q('[data-deltaval]').textContent = (delta > 0 ? '+' : '') + delta;
      const O = outcomes(delta);
      const one = evalSet(O, n, runSeed(run));
      q('[data-one]').textContent = `old ${pts(one.po)}% · new ${pts(one.pn)}% · diff ${signed(one.mean)} pts · 95% interval ${signed(one.lo)} to ${signed(one.hi)}`;
      const verdictOne = one.lo > 0 ? 'The interval is above zero: this eval says better.' : one.hi < 0 ? 'The interval is below zero: this eval says worse.' : 'The interval includes zero: this eval cannot tell better from worse.';
      q('[data-onenote]').textContent = `eval #${run + 1}: the new model fixed ${one.b} items and broke ${one.c}; only those carry information. ${verdictOne} Gate: ${GATES[gate](one) ? 'ship' : 'block'}.`;
      const s = study(O, n, gate); const td = O.trueDiff;
      let wrongText; let note; let bad = false;
      if (td <= -NOISE_BAND) {
        wrongText = `${s.ship} of ${TRIALS} (${Math.floor((s.ship * 100) / TRIALS)}%) shipped a real regression`; bad = s.ship * WRONG_DIV > TRIALS;
        note = `true gap ${signed(td)} pts; the gate should block it every time`;
      } else if (td >= NOISE_BAND) {
        const miss = TRIALS - s.ship; wrongText = `${miss} of ${TRIALS} (${Math.floor((miss * 100) / TRIALS)}%) blocked a real improvement`; bad = miss * WRONG_DIV > TRIALS;
        note = `true gap ${signed(td)} pts; the gate should ship it every time`;
      } else {
        wrongText = `no wrong call: shipped ${s.ship} of ${TRIALS}`;
        note = `true gap ${signed(td, 2)} pts is inside the 1 point noise band, so either call is harmless`;
      }
      q('[data-wrong]').textContent = wrongText; q('[data-wrongnote]').textContent = note;
      q('[data-gatebox]').style.setProperty('--c', bad ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--role-2)');
      q('[data-width]').textContent = `${pts(s.width)} pts`;
      const v = q('[data-verdict]'); v.classList.toggle('bad', bad);
      if (td <= -NOISE_BAND) v.textContent = bad
        ? `With ${n} items this gate lets a ${pts(-td)} point regression through ${Math.floor((s.ship * 100) / TRIALS)}% of the time. The interval is ${pts(s.width)} points wide, wider than the effect you are trying to see.`
        : `With ${n} items this gate catches the ${pts(-td)} point regression in ${TRIALS - s.ship} of ${TRIALS} evals. Interval width is ${pts(s.width)} points.`;
      else if (td >= NOISE_BAND) v.textContent = bad
        ? `The new model really is ${pts(td)} points better, but with ${n} items this gate blocks it in ${Math.floor(((TRIALS - s.ship) * 100) / TRIALS)}% of evals. The set is too small to show the win, or the bar is too strict for its size.`
        : `The ${pts(td)} point improvement ships in ${s.ship} of ${TRIALS} evals. Interval width is ${pts(s.width)} points.`;
      else v.textContent = `The models are within noise (true gap ${signed(td, 2)} pts). Whatever one eval says, it is mostly luck: the interval is ${pts(s.width)} points wide.`;
      rows.forEach((r, k) => {
        const e = evalSet(O, n, TRIAL_SEED.base + k * TRIAL_SEED.step); const ship = GATES[gate](e);
        r.lab.textContent = `${String(k + 1).padStart(2, '0')} ${ship ? 'ship ' : 'block'}`;
        const a = pos(e.lo), b = pos(e.hi);
        r.bar.style.left = a + '%'; r.bar.style.width = Math.max(0.8, b - a) + '%';
        r.bar.classList.toggle('ship', ship); r.dot.style.left = pos(e.mean) + '%';
      });
    }
    function schedule() { if (scheduled) return; scheduled = true; requestAnimationFrame(draw); }
    q('[data-n]').addEventListener('change', () => { run = 0; schedule(); });
    q('[data-delta]').addEventListener('input', () => { run = 0; schedule(); });
    q('[data-gate]').addEventListener('change', schedule);
    q('[data-again]').addEventListener('click', () => { run++; schedule(); });
    q('[data-reset]').addEventListener('click', () => { q('[data-n]').value = '100'; q('[data-delta]').value = '-3'; q('[data-gate]').value = 'point'; run = 0; schedule(); });
    draw();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .mev-rows { display: grid; gap: 3px; }
  .playground .mev-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 8px; align-items: center; }
  .playground .mev-lab { white-space: pre; }
  .playground .mev-track { position: relative; height: 12px; background: var(--surface-2); border-radius: 6px; }
  .playground .mev-zero { position: absolute; left: 50%; top: -2px; bottom: -2px; width: 2px; background: var(--text); }
  .playground .mev-bar { position: absolute; top: 3px; height: 6px; border-radius: 3px; border: 1px solid var(--muted); background: transparent; box-sizing: border-box; }
  .playground .mev-bar.ship { background: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); }
  .playground .mev-dot { position: absolute; top: 1px; width: 4px; height: 10px; margin-left: -2px; background: var(--text); border-radius: 2px; }
</style>
